# Ivan S. Titov <iohann.s.titov@gmail.com> (2026-04-20)
# IPX was removed from the Linux kernel in 4.18 (2018). Userspace utils
# are only useful with the out-of-tree ipx module. Keep but mask.
net-misc/ipx-utils

# Ivan S. Titov <iohann.s.titov@gmail.com> (2026-04-20)
# Upstream (github.com/megabaks) dormant since 2014-02. No tagged
# release, 9999-only. Keep but mask.
app-portage/portopts

# Ivan S. Titov <iohann.s.titov@gmail.com> (2026-04-22)
# ::gentoo qscintilla-2.14.1-r2 dropped Qt5 support; only -r1, revived in
# this overlay, still builds libqscintilla2_qt5. sci-physics/mantid keeps a
# qt5 USE flag beside the default qt6 one, and mantid[qt5] needs that
# library, so the trigger for lifting this mask is mantid losing IUSE=qt5 -
# not mantid defaulting to qt6, which already happened at 6.16.1.1.
# re-verified 2026-07-28
=x11-libs/qscintilla-2.14.1-r2

# Ivan S. Titov <iohann.s.titov@gmail.com> (2026-06-08)
# Last of the 1.x series before the 2.0 rewrite; retained as a recovery
# ebuild but blocked from default install. Remove this mask if a 1.x
# rollback becomes relevant again.
=app-portage/portconf-1.6.8

# Ivan S. Titov <iohann.s.titov@gmail.com> (2026-08-23)
# Beta desktop UI (Tauri). This -bin ships only the GUI shell; on first
# launch unsloth-studio downloads its own uv, a private CPython, PyTorch and
# the inference engine into ~/.unsloth/studio, entirely outside portage - it
# does not use the system sci-ml/unsloth / sci-ml/pytorch stack. Masked so
# users opt in to that runtime self-bootstrap (and the beta status)
# consciously. Lift once a version reuses system packages, or drop the beta tag.
sci-ml/unsloth-desktop-bin

# Ivan S. Titov <iohann.s.titov@gmail.com> (2026-08-29)
# ROCm 10.0 split stack -- COMPLETE and build-verified on gfx1150, base,
# runtime and math libraries alike.
#
# Masked because these share SLOT 0 with the 7.2.x stack: an unmasked world
# update would upgrade them piecemeal, and the subslot flips from 0/7.2 to
# 0/10.0 (four ebuilds pin dev-util/hipcc with :=). Lift the whole block at
# once, never individual entries.
#
# Building any of these needs BOTH a local -llvm_slot_23 in
# /etc/portage/profile/use.mask (::gentoo keyworded LLVM 23.1.0 on 2026-08-29
# but still USE-masks that flag profile-wide, which is a separate gate from
# keywording) and llvm_slot_23 enabled per package -- my.use pins the ROCm
# packages to llvm_slot_20/22, which the 10.0 versions cannot satisfy.
#
# The math libraries additionally need USE=amd-llvm on dev-util/hipcc, which
# points `hipconfig --hipclangpath` at llvm-core/rocm-llvm and so redirects
# rocm.eclass's rocm_use_clang(). AMD builds ROCm against its own LLVM fork,
# and the divergences are compiler-level rather than packaging defects --
#
#   composable-kernel  amd_wmma.hpp passes bhalf16_t (__bf16 vector) to
#                      __builtin_amdgcn_wmma_f32_16x16x16_bf16_w32, which
#                      vanilla clang 23 declares as taking
#                      short __attribute__((ext_vector_type(16))).
#   hipBLASLt          TensileLite GENERATES gfx1150 assembly the vanilla
#                      assembler rejects ("operands are not valid for this GPU
#                      or mode" on v_max_f16 with an abs() source modifier);
#                      being generated, it cannot be patched away.
#   rocBLAS            same class, via Tensile: "operands are not valid for
#                      this GPU or mode" on v_cvt_f16_f32.
#
# dev-util/rocm_bandwidth_test stays at 7.2.4 -- verified 2026-08-30 that no
# 10.0 source exists (no asset in rocm-systems therock-10.0, and its own repo
# stops at rocm-7.2.4). No longer a blocker: 7.2.4-r1 replaces its pins on
# rocr-runtime and hip with :=, so it rebuilds across the subslot flip instead
# of refusing to solve against it. The unrevisioned 7.2.4 keeps the old 0/7.2
# pin and remains only as a rollback target -- an exact pin to it still blocks
# the lift.
#
# llvm-core/rocm-llvm is in the block for a different reason than the rest. It
# has no 7.2.x version, so neither the piecemeal-upgrade nor the subslot-flip
# argument above applies to it. It is here because it is reachable only through
# dev-util/hipcc[amd-llvm], it RDEPENDs the masked rocm-device-libs:0/10.0, and
# it is a ~30G full-LLVM build -- unmasked, `emerge llvm-core/rocm-llvm` would
# be permitted and then fail at resolution instead of reporting a mask.
#
# dev-util/therock-bin remains an alternative: it bundles AMD's clang 23.
=dev-build/rocm-cmake-10.0.0
=dev-libs/rocm-core-10.0.0
=dev-libs/hipother-10.0.0
=dev-libs/roct-thunk-interface-10.0.0
=dev-libs/rocm-device-libs-10.0.0
=dev-libs/rocm-comgr-10.0.0
=dev-libs/rocr-runtime-10.0.0
=dev-libs/rocm-opencl-runtime-10.0.0
=dev-libs/rccl-10.0.0
=dev-util/hipcc-10.0.0
=dev-util/hip-10.0.0
=dev-util/hipify-clang-10.0.0
=dev-util/rocm-smi-10.0.0
=dev-util/rocminfo-10.0.0
=dev-util/Tensile-10.0.0
=dev-util/roctracer-10.0.0
=llvm-core/rocm-llvm-10.0.0
=sci-libs/hipBLAS-common-10.0.0
=sci-libs/rocPRIM-10.0.0
=sci-libs/rocRAND-10.0.0
=sci-libs/hipCUB-10.0.0
=sci-libs/rocThrust-10.0.0
=sci-libs/hipRAND-10.0.0
=sci-libs/rocBLAS-10.0.0
=sci-libs/rocFFT-10.0.0
=sci-libs/rocSPARSE-10.0.0
=sci-libs/miopen-10.0.0
=sci-libs/hipFFT-10.0.0
=sci-libs/rocSOLVER-10.0.0
=sci-libs/hipSPARSE-10.0.0
=sci-libs/hipBLAS-10.0.0
=sci-libs/hipSOLVER-10.0.0
